  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Oral bioavailability is 64%, and a standard morning meal does not change it. Over 99% is bound to plasma proteins, and the drug leaves almost entirely through bile.",
    "substance": "A monosodium salt that is a hygroscopic powder, freely soluble in water; the active moiety has a molecular weight of 586.2.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA as 10 mg tablets, 4 and 5 mg chewable tablets and 4 mg oral granules, dosed once daily.",
    "safety": "Boxed warning for serious neuropsychiatric events; contraindicated in hypersensitivity to any component. Upper respiratory infection and headache are the most common reactions.",
    "indication": "Prophylaxis and chronic treatment of asthma, prevention of exercise-induced bronchoconstriction, and relief of allergic rhinitis symptoms.",
    "mechanism": "Binds the CysLT1 receptor with high affinity and selectivity, blocking LTD4 actions there without any agonist activity."
  },
  "tell": "A leukotriene receptor antagonist whose boxed warning covers serious neuropsychiatric events.",
